hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15543","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in al-Najm, and the people prostrated with him. Al-Muttalib said: And I did not prostrate with them, while he was then a mushrik. Al-Muttalib said: So I shall never leave prostration in it ever."
"15544","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us: Rabah narrated to us, from Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Jafar ibn Abi Wadaah al-Sahmi, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in Makkah Surah al-Najm and prostrated, and those with him prostrated. So I raised my head and refused to prostrate, and al-Muttalib had not become Muslim that day, and afterwards he would never hear anyone recite it but he prostrated."
